Based on my research, here is a comprehensive analysis of innovative utilization of surplus and off-grid renewable electricity in remote Indonesian 3T villages (Tertinggal Terdepan Terluar):

## 1. Green Hydrogen Micro-Hubs and Micro-Ammonia for Diesel Replacement

### What Exists Today
- **PLN operates 22 green hydrogen production facilities** across Indonesia with a combined capacity of ~203 tons per year (as of early 2024)
- The facilities are primarily located at geothermal power plants (PLTP) and steam gas power plants (PLTGU)
- **Technology Readiness Level (TRL)**: 5-6 (prototype demonstration in relevant environment)

### What is Piloted
- **Hydrogen Diesel Dual Fuel (H2 DDF) Bus Pilot** on Rote Island (launched July 2026) - demonstrates hydrogen partially replacing fossil fuels in commercial vehicles
- **Green Hydrogen Corridor**: 194-km corridor linking Jakarta (unveiled July 2026)
- **Diesel Replacement Program (DRP)**: PLN's ambitious program to convert ~5,200 diesel power plants (PLTD) to renewable energy, primarily solar PV + battery storage

### Future
- Government plans to accelerate hydrogen use for power generation in remote areas
- Price benchmarks being set below local generation costs to make hydrogen competitive
- Plans for scaling hydrogen production to 100,000 metric tons annually in Sumatra

### Maturity
**Early Pilot to Demonstration Phase (TRL 5-6)**

### Concrete Examples
1. **Kamojang Geothermal Plant**: First green hydrogen production facility in Southeast Asia
   - Source: https://business-indonesia.org/news/green-hydrogen-supply-to-pln-hrs-pltp-kamojang-becomes-the-first-in-southeast-asia

2. **Rote Island H2 DDF Bus Pilot**: Partnership between PLN and other stakeholders to demonstrate hydrogen-diesel dual fuel technology
   - Source: https://www.globalhydrogenreview.com/hydrogen/23072026/indonesia-accelerates-hydrogen-transport-ecosystem/

3. **Muara Karang PLTGU**: New green hydrogen plant in Jakarta producing ~51 tonnes annually
   - Source: https://cesgs.unair.ac.id/callforpaper-asbif2026/pln-starts-green-hydrogen-production/

## 2. Productive-Use-of-Energy Business Models

### Cold Chain
#### What Exists Today
- Solar-powered cold storage units operational in fishing villages
- Solar ice makers producing up to 1 ton of ice per day

#### What is Piloted
- **UNDP ACCESS Project**: Solar water pumps and cold chain solutions in 23 villages across 4 provinces (East Nusa Tenggara, West Sulawesi, South-East Sulawesi, Central Kalimantan)
- **Kawa Village Solar Ice Maker**: Launched October 2024, transforms tuna fishery by boosting incomes and reducing waste
- **Pertamina NRE Solar Cold Storage**: Planned pilot in two coastal villages in Sumatra (early 2026) with expansion to 82 villages

#### Future
- Scaling solar cold chain to more coastal 3T villages
- Integration with renewable energy mini-grids

#### Maturity
**Pilot to Early Commercial (TRL 7-8)**

#### Concrete Examples
1. **Kawa Village, Indonesia**: Solar ice maker improving small-scale fisheries
   - Source: https://www.undp.org/indonesia/press-releases/launch-solar-ice-maker-kawa-village-boost-indonesian-small-scale-fisheries

2. **UNDP ACCESS Project**: 23 villages in Indonesia receiving solar water pumps and cold chain solutions
   - Source: https://www.undp.org/timor-leste/news/game-changer-rural-communities-solar-water-pump-bringing-water-closer-120-households

### Agro-Processing
#### What Exists Today
- Mini-grids enabling ginger and lemongrass cultivation, wood processing
- Community-owned solar mini-grids providing electricity for productive uses

#### What is Piloted
- **MENTARI Project**: 95 kWp community-owned solar and battery mini-grid in Central Sumba (inaugurated August 2022)
- **Muara Enggelam Village**: Solar PV grid supporting livelihoods in East Kalimantan
- **Anekatek and Akuo Energy mini-grids**: In East Sumba and Berau, increasing productive use of electricity

#### Future
- Scaling productive use appliances and business models
- Integration of solar PV with agricultural processing

#### Maturity
**Pilot to Early Commercial (TRL 7-8)**

#### Concrete Examples
1. **Central Sumba Mini-Grid**: 95 kWp community-owned solar and battery system
   - Source: https://mentari.info/2022/08/24/mentari-uk-indonesia-low-carbon-energy-partnership-inauguration-of-a-95-kwp-community-owned-solar-and-battery-mini-grid-in-central-sumba/

2. **Sumba Island Productive Uses**: Ginger and lemongrass cultivation, wood processing enabled by mini-grids
   - Source: https://www.climatepolicyinitiative.org/electrifying-the-last-mile-community-based-renewable-energy-for-eastern-indonesia/

### Water Pumps
#### What Exists Today
- Solar-powered water pumping systems (PATS) deployed in various locations
- UNDP ACCESS project providing solar water pumps in multiple provinces

#### What is Piloted
- **Solar Home & Pumping System (SHPS) Scheme**: For lighting and clean water access in 3T regions
- **Nunleu Village Solar Water Pump**: Designed to help with clean water distribution

#### Future
- Expansion of solar irrigation systems to combat drought
- Integration with mini-grids for water pumping

#### Maturity
**Commercial (TRL 9)**

#### Concrete Examples
1. **UNDP ACCESS Solar Water Pumps**: 23 villages in 4 Indonesian provinces
   - Source: https://www.undp.org/timor-leste/news/game-changer-rural-communities-solar-water-pump-bringing-water-closer-120-households

2. **IESR Solar-Powered Water Pumps (PATS)**: Four types tailored to land characteristics
   - Source: https://iesr.or.id/en/solar-powered-water-pumps-pats-promote-energy-independence-and-food-security/

### Digital Kiosks
#### What Exists Today
- Solar-powered kiosks operating in 30 villages in Sumba
- Over 2,000 chargeable lanterns distributed

#### What is Piloted
- **New Energy Nexus Smart Solar-Powered Kiosks**: Empowering small business owners in Indonesia
- Kiosks providing battery charging, home lighting system sales and rentals

#### Future
- Expansion to more 3T villages
- Integration with digital services and financial inclusion

#### Maturity
**Pilot to Early Commercial (TRL 7-8)**

#### Concrete Examples
1. **Sumba Island Solar Kiosks**: 30 villages with solar-powered kiosks
   - Source: https://newenergynexus.id/news/smart-solar-powered-kiosks-are-empowering-small-business-owners-in-indonesia/

### E-Mobility
#### What Exists Today
- Limited specific off-grid e-mobility in 3T villages
- Indonesia's broader EV ambitions: 600,000 four-wheel BEVs and 13 million electric motorcycles by 2030

#### What is Piloted
- **Hydrogen-Diesel Dual Fuel Bus Pilot** on Rote Island (July 2026)
- Limited electric motorcycle and vehicle charging infrastructure development

#### Future
- Off-grid EV charging stations powered by renewable energy
- E-mobility integrated with renewable mini-grids in 3T villages

#### Maturity
**Early Pilot (TRL 5-6)**

#### Concrete Examples
1. **Rote Island H2 DDF Bus**: Partnership with PLN for hydrogen mobility
   - Source: https://www.globalhydrogenreview.com/hydrogen/23072026/indonesia-accelerates-hydrogen-transport-ecosystem/

## 3. Agrivoltaics

### What Exists Today
- Research papers on agrivoltaics in Indonesia (15 research papers identified)
- Studies on peanuts, tomatoes, and green beans tolerating partial shading
- Mostly academic/research phase with limited commercial deployment

### What is Piloted
- No specific pilot projects in 3T villages identified yet
- Research conducted primarily in Sumatra and Java

### Future
- Potential for agrivoltaics in 3T regions with agricultural communities
- Integration with existing solar PV deployments

### Maturity
**Research to Early Pilot (TRL 3-4)**

### Concrete Examples
1. **Agrivoltaics Research in Indonesia**: Studies on crop tolerance to partial shading
   - Source: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/395426654_Agrivoltaics_systems_in_Indonesia_Opportunities_challenges_and_lessons_from_other_countries

2. **WRI Report on Agrivoltaics in Asia**: Indonesia identified as having potential but limited deployment
   - Source: https://www.wri.org/insights/agrivoltaics-energy-food-production-asia

## 4. Transactive Energy and Micro-Grid P2P Trading Between Village Clusters

### What Exists Today
- Research and stakeholder perception studies on blockchain-based P2P energy trading
- Tri Mumpuni (Ibu Puni) has brought electricity to at least 61 remote villages in Indonesia

### What is Piloted
- **Gumelar District P2P Energy Trading Pilot**: Blockchain-based P2P energy trading model using blockchain technology
- Research on implementation frameworks for blockchain-based P2P renewable energy trading in Indonesia

### Future
- Scaling P2P trading between village clusters
- Integration with national grid when available
- Digital platforms for energy trading in remote communities

### Maturity
**Research to Pilot (TRL 4-5)**

### Concrete Examples
1. **Gumelar District P2P Trading Study**: Stakeholder perceptions of blockchain-based P2P energy trading
   - Source: https://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/17/19/4956

2. **Tri Mumpuni's Work**: 61 remote villages electrified, with potential for P2P trading models
   - Source: https://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/17/19/4956

3. **Blockchain Implementation Framework**: Research on smart implementation framework for P2P renewable energy trading
   - Source: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/390322949_Developing_a_Smart_Implementation_Framework_for_Blockchain-Based_P2P_Renewable_Energy_Trading_in_Indonesia_A_Qualitative_Analysis_Approach

## 5. Digital Value Export via RWA Tokenization or Carbon Credits

### What Exists Today
- Indonesia opened carbon trading market in October 2023
- Verra preparing to issue first credits under Indonesia's new carbon market regulations (July 2026)
- Blockchain-based renewable energy certificate system being researched

### What is Piloted
- **Verra Carbon Credits**: Three Indonesian forestry projects preparing for credit issuance
- **Blockchain-based REC System**: Research showing blockchain can revolutionize Indonesian REC market
- **Carbon Pricing**: Indonesia's carbon tax at 69,600 rupiah ($4.45) per metric ton

### Future
- Tokenization of renewable energy certificates and carbon credits
- RWA (Real World Asset) tokenization for energy assets in 3T villages
- Digital platforms for exporting carbon value when electrons cannot be exported to PLN

### Maturity
**Early Pilot to Demonstration (TRL 4-6)**

### Concrete Examples
1. **Verra Carbon Credits**: First credits under Indonesia's new regulations
   - Source: https://verra.org/verra-to-issue-first-credits-under-indonesias-new-carbon-market-regulations/

2. **Blockchain-based REC System**: Research on revolutionizing Indonesian REC market
   - Source: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11847093/

3. **Indonesia Carbon Market**: Opened to both skepticism and hope (October 2023)
   - Source: https://news.mongabay.com/2023/10/indonesia-opens-carbon-trading-market-to-both-skepticism-and-hope/

